  "title": "Pickled Cabbage",
  "description": null,
  "editorial": {
    "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>For my version of pickled cabbage, cabbage and carrots are marinated with vinegar. This is an easy recipe and ready to eat the next day!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe {\"id\":21567,\"template\":\"chic-template-english\",\"updated\":1733127157142} -->\n<!--WPRM Recipe 21567-->\n<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe\">\n\t<h2 class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-name\">Pickled Cabbage</h2>\n\t<img class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-image\" src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/IMG_7587-3.Blog_-150x150.png\"/>\t<p class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-summary\">\n\t\t\t</p>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-equipment\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-ingredients\">\n\t\t<ul><li>3-4 lb cabbage</li><li>3-4 carrots</li><li>1 head of garlic</li><li>4 cup  water</li><li>1/4 cup  sugar</li><li>2 Tbsp salt</li><li>1/2 cup vegetable oil</li><li>1 cup 6% vinegar</li></ul>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-instructions\">\n\t\t<ol><li>Cut, core and shred cabbage finely.\r\n<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/IMG_7466.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Peel the carrots and grate.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/IMG_7478.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Peel the garlic and cut each clove into 4 pieces.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/IMG_7486.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Place vegetables in a mason jar. <br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/IMG_7485-2.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Meanwhile, in a large pot, boil water with salt, sugar and olive oil. \r\nRemove from the heat and add vinegar. <br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/IMG_7490-2.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Pour hot marinade over the cabbage and let it cool completely.\r\n<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/IMG_7494.Blog_.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Cover with tight lid and store it in the refrigerator. Cabbage will be ready in 12 hours.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/IMG_7587-3.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li></ol>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-notes\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta\">\n\t\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta-course\">Salads</div>\t</div>\n</div>\n<!--End WPRM Recipe-->\n<!-- /wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe -->",
    "excerpt": null
  },
